WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.621
The year 2045. Genesis has no energy left for
another journey.

2
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.189
Did you do it?

3
00:00:07.209 --> 00:00:08.798
I don't know. Look.

4
00:00:10.383 --> 00:00:16.038
From the window, the Earth looks different.
Some regions have regained their green and

5
00:00:16.058 --> 00:00:20.281
some seas are blue again. And others are still
covered in smoke.

6
00:00:34.383 --> 00:00:39.862
The records changed in many places. But it
wasn't enough to prevent the collapse everywhere.

7
00:00:39.882 --> 00:00:41.875
Was everything we did for nothing?

8
00:00:41.895 --> 00:00:47.404
It wasn't for nothing. Every place that was
reached in time is a page that changed. But

9
00:00:47.424 --> 00:00:51.236
recovery needs sustained, collective action,
on every front.

10
00:00:52.517 --> 00:00:58.530
Some pages of the notebook changed. The last
one, Killa's, is still the same.

11
00:01:10.517 --> 00:01:16.917
My grandma says the river used to warn us.
That night, nobody warned us.

12
00:01:17.983 --> 00:01:18.760
Someday.

13
00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:20.203
Someday we'll go.

14
00:01:31.383 --> 00:01:35.547
Every decision matters. But none is enough on
its own.

15
00:01:35.817 --> 00:01:43.917
In the game, the last return is gone. Out here
there is no time machine. There is data, and
it's still today.

16
00:01:43.937 --> 00:01:49.206
You can read it before it's too late, check it
against a second source, and go out and share it.

17
00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:56.907
TERRA 2045. The future is not written. But
every decision leaves a mark.
